(d)  the padding identity:  P = l*q with l a variable not occurring in q.
     Euler for q of degree 3 gives Hess(q).x = 2.grad(q), and q(x) = 0
     gives grad(q).x = 0; the bordered determinant
        det [[0, g^T],[g, x_0 K]] = -det(x_0 K) * g^T (x_0 K)^{-1} g
     is then -det(x_0 K) * (grad q . x) / (2 x_0) = 0.
     So det Hess(l*q) vanishes identically on {q = 0}: any such padded
     form has dual defect at least 1, with no hypothesis on q.
     Checked above: rank 9, never 10, at 8 independent points.

